{
  "_comment": [
    "Manifest for Scripts/leeloo.py. Data, not code: extend coverage here.",
    "",
    "Fields per row:",
    "  id              claim-sheet row id",
    "  tier            A cheap (<5s) | B moderate (<2min) | C expensive (>2min)",
    "  claims          the figure or verdict directives/claim-sheet.md currently states",
    "  label           human description",
    "  cmd             argv list, run with cwd = repo root",
    "  approx_seconds  single-pass estimate, used only for the time estimate",
    "  note            anything a future maintainer needs to know",
    "",
    "Commands are taken verbatim from REPROduce.md with the `| tee` removed,",
    "because leeloo captures stdout itself. Rows whose command no longer exists",
    "or which time superseded code paths are marked lineage:true and skipped.",
    "",
    "Tier C rows are hours. That is fine; leeloo is resumable (--resume).",
    "",
    "Tier D = STATISTICAL, not timing. These rows report eps (Gaussian ingest",
    "failure log2) and sigma-hat estimated from a handful of trials. The sheet",
    "itself flags several as 'sample-sensitive': C32 moves -32 -> -8.4 between 4",
    "and 8 trials; C41 moves -696 -> -76.6 between 2 and 4. Since eps <= 2^-64 is",
    "a pass/fail security bar, sample variance here is scientifically load-bearing",
    "in a way that a 5% timing spread is not. C35 sits 1.4 from the bar at n=4.",
    "Run these with --runs 3+ and read the SPREAD OF EPS, not the wall clock.",
    "",
    "Tier D approx_seconds corrected 2026-08-15 from measured cost:",
    "N=1024 covering-b1 (l=32) is 155 s/TRIAL, covering-b2 (l=16) ~75 s/trial,",
    "N=128 is 0.21 s/trial. The first estimates were ~10x low.",
    "",
    "approx_seconds corrected to measured PROCESS wall (not the tool's own",
    "reported wall) 2026-08-15. C52 for example reports 43 s internally but the",
    "process takes 280 s, and it is process time that a sweep actually costs."
  ],
